# Changelog
All notable changes to this project are documented here. This project adheres to semantic versioning.

## [1.6.0]
### Added
- Custom post type support. A Settings > PageScale screen lets you choose which post types PageScale manages.
- A Scalable Manager screen per managed post type, with a switcher when more than one type is enabled.
- Automatic tree-vs-flat view: hierarchical types keep the parent/child tree; non-hierarchical types get the flat virtual list.
### Changed
- Duplicate now inherits the source item's post type and copies that type's taxonomies.
- Total and parents caches are keyed per post type.
- Permission checks validate against each post type's own capabilities.
### Fixed
- Duplicating an Elementor page no longer corrupts its layout: copied meta is slashed correctly and per-post builder CSS caches are regenerated for the copy.
- A duplicated page now gets a unique slug (e.g. privacy-policy-2) while the original keeps its slug unchanged.
- Quick edit saves are slashed correctly and surface a clear error if a page-builder save hook fails.
- Permanent deletion from trash verifies the result and recovers when a corrupted builder payload blocks deletion.
- Quick edit and drag-and-drop reparenting save over POST instead of PATCH; several hosting stacks block PATCH at the server, so saves silently failed.
- The virtual-scroll repaint no longer resets an open quick-edit form; in-progress values are preserved across repaints.
- Taxonomy term changes in quick edit now save; the capability check used a non-existent capability name and always failed.
- The Scalable Manager submenu now attaches correctly under the built-in Posts menu.

## [1.5.1]
### Security
- Apply private-page readability filtering to the /parents, /export and /default-view REST endpoints.
- Cache the parents list per user to avoid serving one user's readable set to another.

## [1.5.0]
### Added
- Lazy, one-at-a-time FULLTEXT index building to avoid gateway timeouts on large tables.
- Optional content and custom-field FULLTEXT search behind a UI toggle.
- Elementor-aware quick actions.
- Duplicate detection and CSV export endpoints.
### Changed
- Keyset (cursor) pagination replaces offset-based paging for constant per-request cost.

## [1.0.0]
### Added
- Initial release: lazy hierarchy tree, virtual-scroll list, tiered indexed search, custom REST namespace.
